  "title": "Healthy Brain Network (HBN) EEG - Release 3",
  "description": "Release 3 of the HBN-EEG dataset, the EEG component of the Child Mind Institute Healthy Brain Network project, organized in BIDS format. It contains EEG recordings and behavioral responses from 183 children and young people performing three passive tasks (resting state, surround suppression, movie watching) and three active tasks (contrast change detection, sequence learning, symbol search). Events carry HED annotations, and the participants file includes quality-control results and psychopathology factors derived from the CBCL questionnaire.",
  "methods_description": "Participants aged 5-21 completed six EEG tasks: resting state with eyes open and closed, surround suppression, movie watching, contrast change detection, sequence learning, and symbol search. Behavioral responses were merged into the events.tsv files, which are HED-annotated. Minimal quality control checked for file corruption and the presence of required events.",
